 \section{ProtoHedge and the Empirical Validation Problem}
 \label{sec:protohedge_empirical_problem}
 
-This section places our study in context. We first summarize the deep hedging framework and the role of vanilla Deep Hedging as the main black-box benchmark. We then explain the ProtoHedge architecture and its interpretability motivation. Finally, we identify the central gap left by the original ProtoHedge study: although prototype-based hedging is attractive conceptually, it must still be shown to remain competitive and interpretable on real historical market data.
